  "verbalization": "Deflazacort is implicated in the pathogenesis of Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy (DMD) through a series of interconnected indications. The drug is linked to DMD via three distinct pathways, all of which ultimately lead to a connection with Muscular Dystrophy. Eteplirsen, Golodirsen, and Ataluren are approved treatments for DMD, and Deflazacort is indicated for the same condition, suggesting a potential therapeutic overlap. The shared indication for DMD and the final indication for Muscular Dystrophy imply a conceptual link between Deflazacort and the broader class of therapies targeting DMD. The evidence suggests that Deflazacort may be repurposed for Muscular Dystrophy due to its association with DMD and the presence of similar therapeutic targets, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Deflazacort to play a role in the treatment of muscular dystrophy through its involvement in the therapeutic landscape of DMD.",
